        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                "word": "mitigation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b129c9c3-763b-45bf-89b4-381efbbdca92",
                        "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mitigations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afac6a00-6ffa-31b7-ab6a-aa03347db1b0",
                        "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Adoucissement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "429164a8-4bf6-46c9-b841-de20104670fc",
                                "sense_id": "afac6a00-6ffa-31b7-ab6a-aa03347db1b0",
                                "text": "La mitigation des peines de l’enfer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d980c61-171e-41f1-b1ec-967b0e6dff8e",
                                "sense_id": "afac6a00-6ffa-31b7-ab6a-aa03347db1b0",
                                "text": "L’homme est lent, peu rigoureux et très intuitif. L’ordinateur est super rapide, très rigoureux et complètement con. On essaie de faire des programmes qui font une mitigation entre les deux. Le but est louable. Mais de là à y arriver…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1499e36-dcb3-34ef-8cf4-90f3a8e12436",
                        "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Réduction des nuisances créées par les activités spatiales, qui affectent les missions spatiales ou l’environnement terrestre et spatial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a96a0ff-76a9-4b01-90cf-40b7ead7f150",
                                "sense_id": "f1499e36-dcb3-34ef-8cf4-90f3a8e12436",
                                "text": "Dans un horizon plus lointain, la situation ne pourra se stabiliser durablement que si les acteurs modifient leurs comportements en profondeur (ce que les Anglo-Saxons appellent mitigation) (...) La littérature identifie deux dimensions dans le méta-problème des débris spatiaux : la mitigation (ne plus produire de nouveaux débris) et la remediation (nettoyer les débris existants)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ad5cf82-a90c-337b-9b7d-ae9066505a47",
                        "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Atténuation d’une atteinte à l’environnement obtenue par la mise en œuvre de dispositions et de mesures appropriées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "443bf462-1c50-484a-9a8d-9142cdbfc7de",
                                "sense_id": "5ad5cf82-a90c-337b-9b7d-ae9066505a47",
                                "text": "À la COP de Charm el-Cheikh, en 2022, un fonds a été créé, le premier du genre, qui n’est destiné ni à la mitigation, ni à l’adaptation, ni à des actions préventives, mais à la compensation des pertes et dommages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02c23dda-38a1-46c9-9b5f-b386217b105f",
                                "sense_id": "5ad5cf82-a90c-337b-9b7d-ae9066505a47",
                                "text": "L'atténuation (on parle aussi de mitigation) désigne dans ce contexte la réduction de la vulnérabilité, des mesures visant à atténuer les impacts des modifications environnementales (conditions climatiques par exemple) sur la société et l’environnement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0848f771-7120-4c92-8e6c-41c75a644f07",
                                "sense_id": "5ad5cf82-a90c-337b-9b7d-ae9066505a47",
                                "text": "Toutefois, le « risque zéro » n’existant pas, la mitigation consiste à réduire la fragilité des enjeux, et non à la supprimer."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71cde9a5-06e4-364f-82fa-f5cbfe1d0f36",
                        "entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ensemble des mesures managériales, techniques, structurelles, financier, etc. prévues (plan de gestion des risques) ou mises en œuvre (curatif) pour atténuer les conséquences d’une situation à risque pour un projet (que faire si les serveurs tombent ? que faire si untel est malade ? comment restaurer les données en cas de problème ? doit-on augmenter les effectifs ? etc.)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eb22bf7-7445-4ad4-b247-49094f80c443",
                                "sense_id": "71cde9a5-06e4-364f-82fa-f5cbfe1d0f36",
                                "text": "Les voies de sorties sont étroites et les firmes disposent de trois moyens pour gérer les risques : supprimer l'origine du risque (prévention), mettre en place des mécanismes d'autoprotection (réduire la probabilité d'apparition) ou mettre en place des mécanismes de mitigation (réduction des conséquences néfastes)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04afb019-1ebe-480f-9e28-584d99bf446d",
                        "source_entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Eingrenzung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01dfa2b0-f200-4737-bb68-f709316cad01",
                        "source_entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "target_lang_word": "mitigation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mitigation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                        "entry_id": "64993727-357e-37a5-bcd2-81b98a4092c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reduction or decrease of something harmful or unpleasant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c10c3f6f-b55f-4c30-96fd-6b8df97f0a37",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Two golden hours, in which the astonishing news of the intended party was revealed to Louisa, with all of its contrivances, expenses, and mitigations, so far as they were elucidated, were given and said to be \"done in her honour;\"..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f671c655-56bd-45c9-a73d-fda9a1487f03",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "One possible drought mitigation strategy for Afghanistan is to divert excess water from water-rich river basins to water-scarce river basins in cases where this is technologically, economically and environmentally feasible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02e96060-23e6-49aa-982e-f780a99f6f30",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Much of the arable land acquired by HS2 is being used for mitigation planting, in an attempt to achieve the goal set by HS2 Ltd for Phase 1, which will mean there should be no measurable loss of biodiversity after construction of the line compared with what was there before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d747c713-8591-45d2-8015-b6a36ccb0932",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Its [the gantry crane's] noise-mitigation characteristics even include a soft-landing feature to minimise the noise when containers are lowered."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7572f51e-e55a-4e3c-abab-0198c6d1b282",
                        "source_entry_id": "440031f7-2b56-366c-a0d6-8d2c1bae603a",
                        "target_lang_word": "palliation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "palliation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31f2915a-6fa9-355a-8980-2222d99381ed",
                                        "entry_id": "2608e85f-54ce-3323-947e-6ad8e97ace7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The alleviation of a disease's symptoms without a cure; temporary relief."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48da5e44-c748-4436-a1ad-1b7ae94ec475",
                                                "sense_id": "31f2915a-6fa9-355a-8980-2222d99381ed",
                                                "text": "The most rapid and most seductive transition in all human nature is that which attends the palliation of a ravenous appetite. There is something humiliating about it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90c76271-94d3-4da6-92e8-bae54b3023c1",
                                                "sense_id": "31f2915a-6fa9-355a-8980-2222d99381ed",
                                                "text": "Una nox dormienda means that one final night that has to be slept through after a few score years of pain and its palliations, of pleasure and disgust after pleasure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc09d356-4493-3b84-9281-97268160f7fe",
                                        "entry_id": "2608e85f-54ce-3323-947e-6ad8e97ace7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Extenuation; mitigation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8a5607b-af9b-4bfd-8ef5-93f32acc2e70",
                                                "sense_id": "cc09d356-4493-3b84-9281-97268160f7fe",
                                                "text": "The strong hand of the law is around your life and your wealth, but he who takes from you all that renders them valuable, the chances are, that his offence will find palliation and excuse; nay, that the laughers will be on his side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
